<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Bradshaw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1916">1916</a>–<a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Bradshaw was a trade unionist and politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> who led the Labour Party that dominated the islands' politics from the 1950s. He served as a minister in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation, and from 1967 as premier of the Associated State of Saint Christopher-Nevis-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anguilla">Anguilla</a>, opposing Anguilla's secession. He died in office in 1978 and is regarded as a national hero.</p></div>
